// teach 5: add with !Alloc
// Two callers stand on `f` not allocating and one on it not trapping: the
// lock more declarations stand on is the one taught (a declaration that
// authors a clause is offered no further lock).
fn f(x) = x + 1

fn a(x) with !Alloc = f(x)

fn b(x) with !Alloc = f(x) + 1

fn c(x) with !Trap = f(x)

fn main() = a(1) + b(2) + c(3)
